12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', '[{"id": "0a8a89e5-5aff-4b5b-847c-93556ccf0299", "phase": "TEACHER", "description": "Model Fourth-generation computers and the microchip slowly, think ... (536 characters truncated) ... e microchip slowly, think aloud, and check that all learners can see and hear.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', "Ask each pair to name two features of fourth-generation computers and point to the microchip on the diagram. Listen for 'microprocessor' and 'smaller' rather than a memorised list. Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation.", "Review the steps for Fourth-generation computers and the microchip, discuss the common problem met and how it was solved, and link to everyday technology. Preview the next lesson ('Components of Computers and Computer Systems').", '[]', '[]', '[]', 'Find one device at home that contains a microchip and write two sentences on what the device does and which feature of modern computers it shows.', 'In pairs, learners label a simple processor diagram and write one sentence on why the microchip changed computers. The teacher checks each pair names both the part and the feature it made possible.', 'Find one device at home that contains a microchip and write two sentences on what the device does and which feature of modern computers it shows.', "Support: Pair learners who need help with a peer 'digital buddy' and provide a numbered step card for Fourth-generation computers and the microchip.\ ... (72 characters truncated) ... eration computers and the microchip to a slightly harder task.\nGrouping: Whole-class demonstration, small groups at shared devices, individual task.", '[]', 'tpl-wapef-approved-plan', '', '', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-29 10:50:15.041024', '2026-09-29 10:50:15.041027')
