2026-09-29 10:51:42,643 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [cached since 87.6s ago] ('a9e9365d-8f5e-44e3-a927-7ef9dbcc1fb0', '970de595-e0df-4b6a-a2fb-28401462c6d8', '27573c9d-0136-4923-a553-981455c867b2', '2c605d7d-c25e-46f5-b4c9-0f77d3b4a61a', None, 1, '2026-09-11', 0, 2, 1, 1, '2026-09-14', 1, '', 'Basic 7', 'ICT', 11, 60, 'Achimota Basic School', 'Persistence Teacher', 'Introduction to Computing', 'Components of Computers and Computer Systems', 'B7.1.1.1', 'B7.1.1.1', '["B7.1.1.1.1"]', '["B7.1.1.1.1"]', 'Fourth-generation computers and the microchip', "Learners' everyday experience related to this activity.", '[{"id": "9c00a086-7584-43df-aa63-464c363354b5", "description": "Learners can discuss fourth-generation computers and the microchip", "indicator_code": "B7.1.1.1.1", "source": "deterministic"}]', 'Learners will recognize and appreciate the beauty, order, and purpose of design in the physical world around them.', 'Shaping our world.', '["God worshiper", "Image reflector"]', 'Creation', '', '[]', '["Personal Computer", "Processor"]', '[]', '["Personal Computer", "Processor"]', 'This lesson focuses on Fourth-generation computers and the microchip.', 'Hold up a microchip (or a clear picture of one) next to a picture of an early room-sized computer. Ask learners which is newer and why, write their reasons on the board, then tell them both are computers.', '[{"id": "5bcb5e52-7653-4314-94b8-aee01125edc9", "phase": "TEACHING AND DEMONSTRATION", "description": "Name the features of fourth-generation compute ... (834 characters truncated) ...  the board or an unplugged model if there are not enough devices for everyone.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', '[{"id": "af5f8ffc-09a5-4a17-98eb-06754ecd6aad", "phase": "LEARNER", "description": "Watch and listen carefully, then describe each step of Fourth-gen ... (531 characters truncated) ...  each step of Fourth-generation computers and the microchip in your own words.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', '[{"id": "f55801df-b9d1-4a16-99bd-4625fb2b7346", "phase": "TEACHER", "description": "Model Fourth-generation computers and the microchip slowly, think ... (536 characters truncated) ... e microchip slowly, think aloud, and check that all learners can see and hear.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', "Ask each pair to name two features of fourth-generation computers and point to the microchip on the diagram. Listen for 'microprocessor' and 'smaller' rather than a memorised list. Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation.", "Review the steps for Fourth-generation computers and the microchip, discuss the common problem met and how it was solved, and link to everyday technology. Preview the next lesson ('Components of Computers and Computer Systems').", '[]', '[]', '[]', 'Find one device at home that contains a microchip and write two sentences on what the device does and which feature of modern computers it shows.', 'In pairs, learners label a simple processor diagram and write one sentence on why the microchip changed computers. The teacher checks each pair names both the part and the feature it made possible.', 'Find one device at home that contains a microchip and write two sentences on what the device does and which feature of modern computers it shows.', "Support: Pair learners who need help with a peer 'digital buddy' and provide a numbered step card for Fourth-generation computers and the microchip.\ ... (72 characters truncated) ... eration computers and the microchip to a slightly harder task.\nGrouping: Whole-class demonstration, small groups at shared devices, individual task.", '[]', 'tpl-wapef-approved-plan', '', '', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.643162', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.643165')
