ription": "Model Input devices: manual and automatic slowly, think aloud, an ... (506 characters truncated) ... d automatic slowly, think aloud, and check that all learners can see and hear.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', "Give each pair four device cards and ask them to sort the cards as manual or automatic, giving one reason per card. Ask two pairs to explain a borderline device and listen for the words 'manual' and 'automatic' used correctly. Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation.", "Review the steps for Input devices: manual and automatic, discuss the common problem met and how it was solved, and link to everyday technology. Preview the next lesson ('Components of Computers and Computer Systems').", '[]', '[]', '[]', 'Find and list three input devices used in your home or community. For each one, say whether it is manual or automatic and what it is used for.', 'Pairs sort the device pictures into manual and automatic groups, write one reason for each group, and state where each device is used. The teacher checks a sample and asks two pairs to justify a borderline device.', 'Find and list three input devices used in your home or community. For each one, say whether it is manual or automatic and what it is used for.', "Support: Pair learners who need help with a peer 'digital buddy' and provide a numbered step card for Input devices: manual and automatic.\nExtension ... (52 characters truncated) ... Input devices: manual and automatic to a slightly harder task.\nGrouping: Whole-class demonstration, small groups at shared devices, individual task.", '[]', 'tpl-wapef-approved-plan', '', '', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.650622', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.650625')
