nd optical storage media slowly, think aloud,  ... (512 characters truncated) ... orage media slowly, think aloud, and check that all learners can see and hear.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', 'Ask each group to name the storage item with the largest capacity on the table and give the evidence from the label. Check that learners can say why an optical disc is read-only while a hard drive can be written many times. Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation.', "Review the steps for Hard drives and optical storage media, discuss the common problem met and how it was solved, and link to everyday technology. Preview the next lesson ('Components of Computers and Computer Systems').", '[]', '[]', '[]', 'Find one storage device at home or school. Write the capacity printed on it, whether it is magnetic or optical, and one advantage of that type of storage.', 'Groups build a comparison table of the hard drive, portable hard drive, CD-ROM and DVD-ROM using the printed capacities and write speeds, then state one strength and one weakness of each. The teacher checks each table has the correct units.', 'Find one storage device at home or school. Write the capacity printed on it, whether it is magnetic or optical, and one advantage of that type of storage.', "Support: Pair learners who need help with a peer 'digital buddy' and provide a numbered step card for Hard drives and optical storage media.\nExtensi ... (56 characters truncated) ... rd drives and optical storage media to a slightly harder task.\nGrouping: Whole-class demonstration, small groups at shared devices, individual task.", '[]', 'tpl-wapef-approved-plan', '', '', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.656997', '2026-09-29 10:51:42.657003')
